This is the clear instructions on how I create an executable game

Step 1: I opened the terminal and wrote javac -d out src/*.java in order to compile my java files.
Step 2: I then copy all of the other packages from my main file (jframe) to the "out", this include "images" package.
(make sure initially we do not have an "out" file already, can delete it if have initially, then make new "out" file.
Step 3: Then I create a manifest file (MANIFEST.MF) using this prompt:

Manifest-Version: 1.0
Main-Class: Santorini

Step 4: I then create the JAR file by typing jar cfm Game.jar MANIFEST.MF -C out . in the terminal.

Step 1 - 4 is how I create a runnable JAR file.

To test whether my Game.jar file can run with my full code or not, i write this command to test run: java -jar Game.jar

Then, I used Launch4j and set my output file to Santorini_vers3.exe. After that, I selected the Game.jar that have just
created from step 1-4 to the "Jar" section. Lastly, I build the generate the exe file named Santorini_vers3. Before that,
I have tested the exe and it is working fine.

In my code, I have used images, so in case the code wont run, change the path of the code to match with the path of image
so that the code can work.